# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "File names {#file-names}"
msgstr "Mga pangalan ng file {#file-names}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use only letters, digits, underscores (`_`), hyphens (`-`), and periods (`.`).** A managed workflow removes other characters, such as spaces, from the name when you download or delete a file. For example, you can upload `my results.json`, but you cannot download it.\n"
msgstr "**Letra, digit, underscore (`_`), hyphen (`-`), at tuldok (`.`) lang ang gamitin.** Inaalis ng managed workflow ang ibang karakter, tulad ng mga espasyo, sa pangalan kapag nag-download o nagbura ka ng file. Halimbawa, maaari mong i-upload ang `my results.json`, pero hindi mo ito ma-download.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**File storage has no folders.** `file_upload()` keeps only the file name, so `inputs/params.json` is stored as `params.json`.\n"
msgstr "**Walang folder ang file storage.** Ang pangalan lang ng file ang itinatago ng `file_upload()`, kaya ang `inputs/params.json` ay sine-save bilang `params.json`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: upload does not sanitize file names, but download and delete do (gateway/api/utils.py sanitize_file_name()). Confirm whether upload should reject or sanitize these names. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read files in a workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Magbasa ng mga file sa workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the name of the file when you run the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang pangalan ng file kapag pinatakbo mo ang workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, edit your workflow code to read the file from `/function_user_data`, which is where every job sees file storage:\n"
msgstr "Para paganahin ito, i-edit ang code ng workflow mo para basahin ang file mula sa `/function_user_data`, kung saan nakikita ng bawat job ang file storage:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inside a job, read and write files through this folder. The client file methods, such as `file_upload()` and `file_download()`, are for your local notebook.\n"
msgstr "Sa loob ng job, magbasa at magsulat ng mga file sa pamamagitan ng folder na ito. Ang mga client file method, tulad ng `file_upload()` at `file_download()`, ay para sa local notebook mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read an archive, extract it to the local disk:\n"
msgstr "Para magbasa ng archive, i-extract ito sa local disk:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write temporary files to `/tmp`. File storage is object storage that the job sees as a folder, so file storage is slower than the local disk. Do heavy reads and writes on the local disk, and copy finished files to file storage.\n"
msgstr "Magsulat ng mga pansamantalang file sa `/tmp`. Ang file storage ay object storage na nakikita ng job bilang folder, kaya mas mabagal ang file storage kaysa sa local disk. Gawin ang mabibigat na pagbasa at pagsulat sa local disk, at kopyahin ang mga natapos na file sa file storage.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm how the mount behaves for appends, renames, and partial writes, and how soon a file that one job writes is visible to a job that is running at the same time. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save output files {#save-output-files}"
msgstr "I-save ang mga output file {#save-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your local notebook reads the names of the output files from the result:\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ng local notebook mo ang mga pangalan ng output file mula sa resulta:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, save each output file at the top level of `/function_user_data`, and return the file names with `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "Para paganahin ito, i-save ang bawat output file sa top level ng `/function_user_data`, at ibalik ang mga pangalan ng file gamit ang `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Files that the job writes outside `/function_user_data`, such as in `/tmp` or the current folder, are deleted when the job ends.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga file na isinusulat ng job sa labas ng `/function_user_data`, gaya ng sa `/tmp` o sa kasalukuyang folder, ay made-delete kapag natapos na ang job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm that the mount stores /function_user_data/<folder>/<file> as the storage key .../data/<folder>/<file>, so that later jobs can read subfolders. file_download() can't fetch these files: sanitize_file_name() strips \"/\", and files() lists only the base name (file_storage_fleets.py get_public_files()). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download output files {#download-output-files}"
msgstr "I-download ang mga output file {#download-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job ends, download each file with `file_download()`. Set `target_name` to choose the local file name, and `download_location` to choose an existing local folder:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos matapos ang job, i-download ang bawat file gamit ang `file_download()`. Itakda ang `target_name` para piliin ang pangalan ng local na file, at ang `download_location` para piliin ang isang umiiral na local na folder:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without `target_name`, `file_download()` adds a random prefix to the local file name, such as `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, and returns the name that it used.\n"
msgstr "Kapag walang `target_name`, nagdaragdag ang `file_download()` ng random na prefix sa pangalan ng local na file, gaya ng `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, at ibinabalik nito ang pangalang ginamit nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download many outputs as one archive {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"
msgstr "I-download ang maraming output bilang isang archive {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a job saves many output files, or files in subfolders, bundle them into one archive in the workflow, and download only the archive:\n"
msgstr "Kung nagse-save ang isang job ng maraming output file, o mga file sa mga subfolder, pagsama-samahin ang mga ito sa isang archive sa workflow, at ang archive lang ang i-download:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, write the outputs to a folder on the local disk, add the folder to an archive in `/tmp`, and copy the archive to file storage:\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ito, isulat ang mga output sa isang folder sa local na disk, idagdag ang folder sa isang archive sa `/tmp`, at kopyahin ang archive sa file storage:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the archive is built on the local disk and copied in one step, file storage never holds an incomplete archive. The archive keeps the folder structure, and it can contain files of any type. In this example, the files are extracted to `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ginagawa ang archive sa local na disk at kinokopya nang sabay-sabay, hindi kailanman magkakaroon ang file storage ng hindi kumpletong archive. Pinapanatili ng archive ang istruktura ng folder, at maaari itong maglaman ng mga file ng anumang uri. Sa halimbawang ito, ang mga file ay ine-extract sa `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete files {#delete-files}"
msgstr "I-delete ang mga file {#delete-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not delete files from file storage, so files remain until you delete them with `file_delete()`:\n"
msgstr "Hindi nagde-delete ng mga file mula sa file storage ang isang managed workflow, kaya nananatili ang mga file hanggang i-delete mo ang mga ito gamit ang `file_delete()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`file_delete()` reports success even if the file does not exist, so check the name with `files()` first. To delete all the files of one run, filter `files()` by the run's name prefix, as described in the next section:\n"
msgstr "Nagre-report ng tagumpay ang `file_delete()` kahit hindi umiiral ang file, kaya tingnan muna ang pangalan gamit ang `files()`. Para i-delete ang lahat ng file ng isang run, i-filter ang `files()` ayon sa prefix ng pangalan ng run, gaya ng inilalarawan sa susunod na seksyon:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: on Fleets, deleting a missing file returns \"Requested file was deleted.\" because gateway/core/ibm_cloud/cos/cos_client.py delete_object() treats a missing key as deleted. Confirm whether file_delete() should return 404 instead. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: give each run's files a unique name {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"
msgstr "Best practice: bigyan ng natatanging pangalan ang mga file ng bawat run {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of your runs of a workflow share the same file storage, and a file that a job saves replaces any stored file with the same name. If you start several runs at the same time and each run saves `energies.npy`, only the last one is kept.\n"
msgstr "Lahat ng run mo ng isang workflow ay nagbabahagi ng parehong file storage, at pinapalitan ng file na sine-save ng isang job ang anumang naka-store na file na may parehong pangalan. Kung magsisimula ka ng ilang run nang sabay at nagse-save ang bawat run ng `energies.npy`, ang huli lang ang mananatili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, pass a run name as an argument, and start the name of every file that the run saves with it:\n"
msgstr "Bilang best practice, magpasa ng pangalan ng run bilang argument, at simulan dito ang pangalan ng bawat file na sine-save ng run:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All runs can read the same input file, `hamiltonian.npz`, because they only read it. Upload a shared input one time, before you start the runs.\n"
msgstr "Lahat ng run ay makakabasa ng parehong input file, `hamiltonian.npz`, dahil binabasa lang nila ito. Mag-upload ng shared na input nang isang beses, bago mo simulan ang mga run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use run names that you can recognize later, and that contain only letters, digits, underscores, hyphens, and periods. With one prefix for each run, you can find, download, and [delete](#delete-files) the files of a run together.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng mga pangalan ng run na makikilala mo sa hinaharap, at naglalaman lang ng mga letra, digit, underscore, hyphen, at tuldok. Sa isang prefix para sa bawat run, mahahanap, ma-di-download, at [made-delete](#delete-files) mo nang sabay ang mga file ng isang run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: checkpoint long jobs {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"
msgstr "Best practice: mag-checkpoint ng mahahabang job {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job that is canceled, fails, or reaches the 24-hour limit loses everything that is not in file storage. For long runs, save a checkpoint to file storage at regular intervals, and resume from it when you run the workflow again with the same run name:\n"
msgstr "Ang job na kinansela, pumalya, o umabot sa 24-oras na limitasyon ay nawawalan ng lahat ng wala sa file storage. Para sa mahahabang run, mag-save ng checkpoint sa file storage sa regular na pagitan, at magpatuloy mula rito kapag pinatakbo mo ulit ang workflow gamit ang parehong pangalan ng run:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To continue a run that stopped, call `run()` again with the same arguments.\n"
msgstr "Para ipagpatuloy ang run na tumigil, tawagin muli ang `run()` gamit ang parehong mga argument.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan ang mga sumusunod na punto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Write the checkpoint to the local disk first, and then copy it.** If the job stops during a write, the stored checkpoint is incomplete, and the next run cannot read it.\n"
msgstr "**Isulat muna ang checkpoint sa local na disk, saka ito kopyahin.** Kung tumigil ang job habang nagsusulat, hindi kumpleto ang naka-store na checkpoint, at hindi ito mababasa ng susunod na run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose an interval that matches the cost of a step.** Save often enough that you do not lose much work, but not so often that writing checkpoints slows the job.\n"
msgstr "**Pumili ng pagitan na tugma sa gastos ng isang hakbang.** Mag-save nang sapat na dalas para hindi masyadong marami ang mawalang trabaho, pero hindi sobrang dalas na babagal ang job dahil sa pagsulat ng mga checkpoint.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete checkpoints after the run succeeds.** A later run with the same name then starts from the beginning.\n"
msgstr "**I-delete ang mga checkpoint pagkatapos magtagumpay ang run.** Magsisimula ulit sa umpisa ang susunod na run na may parehong pangalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a job that is canceled, you can also save partial results in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Para sa job na kinansela, maaari ka ring mag-save ng mga partial na resulta sa isang [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) to start one job for each input.\n"
"- [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) to save partial results when a job is canceled.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- [Magpatakbo ng parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) para magsimula ng isang job para sa bawat input.\n"
"- [Magsulat ng mga log at humawak ng mga error](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) para mag-save ng mga partial na resulta kapag kinansela ang isang job.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
